WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.710
If your prep is SuTab, this video will walk you through exactly how to take it

2
00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:04.720
.

3
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:10.000
Just follow along step by step. Your SuTab kit includes two bottles of 12

4
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.040
tablets each

5
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:16.640
and a measured container. Start your first dose between 6 and 7 pm the night

6
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:17.760
before your procedure.

7
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:23.560
Open your first bottle of 12 tablets. Fill the provided container with 16

8
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:24.640
ounces of water

9
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:30.270
up to the fill line. Swallow one tablet every 2 minutes with a sip of water,

10
00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:31.040
finishing all

11
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:37.120
12 tablets over about 15 to 20 minutes. Take your time and go at a steady pace.

12
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:43.620
About 1 hour after your last tablet, fill the container again with 16 ounces

13
00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:44.320
of water

14
00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.770
and drink the entire amount slowly over 30 minutes. Then, about 30 minutes

15
00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:50.560
after finishing

16
00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:55.470
that container. Fill it one more time with 16 ounces of water and drink the

17
00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:56.880
entire amount over 30

18
00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:04.090
minutes. That completes your first dose. Repeat the exact same three steps

19
00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:05.280
using your second bottle

20
00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.990
of 12 tablets. One tablet every 2 minutes with water, then 16 ounces of water

21
00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:12.320
one hour later,

22
00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:18.000
then 16 ounces of water 30 minutes after that. This part is really important.

23
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:18.720
You must drink

24
00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.430
all of the prep solution as directed, even if you're already passing clear

25
00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:23.040
liquid.

26
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.930
I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose is what gives us

27
00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:28.560
the clearest

28
00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.200
view during your procedure. If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may

29
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.080
need to reschedule

30
00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:38.300
and neither of us wants that. Between doses, keep drinking clear liquids to

31
00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.200
stay hydrated.

32
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:44.090
It will help you feel better and help the prep do its job. Do not drink

33
00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:45.120
anything at all within

34
00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:49.320
4 hours of your procedure, including water, unless it is a small sip to take

35
00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:49.920
a medication.

36
00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:55.280
Your procedure may be canceled or rescheduled if this is not followed. If you

37
00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.080
experience any

38
00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:00.370
discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom, applying a petroleum-based ointment

39
00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:01.200
or diaper

40
00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:07.440
rash cream can really help. That's it. You've got this. Follow the timing,

41
00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:08.560
finish the full dose,

42
00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:13.330
and stay hydrated. If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our

43
00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:13.520
office.

44
00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:15.440
We're here to help.
